---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title       = "Privacy Policy | Rave Wellness";
const description = "How Rave Wellness collects and uses data. We use Google Analytics for traffic measurement and have affiliate relationships with DanceSafe and Amazon.";
const canonical   = "https://www.ravewellness.org/privacy.html";
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} {canonical} ogType="website">
  <Fragment slot="footer-nav">
    <h4>Legal</h4>
    <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>
    <a href="/author/jordan-mercer.html">About</a>
  </Fragment>

  <main>
    <section style="padding: 80px 0 60px;">
      <div class="container" style="max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto;">

        <h1 style="font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 48px;">Last updated: August 13, 2026</p>

        <div class="prose">

          <p>Rave Wellness (<strong>ravewellness.org</strong>) is a harm reduction information site. This policy explains what data we collect, why, and what we do with it. We collect as little as possible and do not sell or share personal data with third parties for advertising purposes.</p>

          <h2 id="what-we-collect-and-why">What we collect and why</h2>

          <h3 id="analytics-google-analytics-4">Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</h3>
          <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how people find and use the site — which pages are read, how long people stay, and what search terms bring them here. This helps us prioritize what content to write and improve.</p>
          <p>Google Analytics collects:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Pages visited and time spent</li>
            <li>Approximate geographic location (country/region, not precise location)</li>
            <li>Device type and browser</li>
            <li>Referring website or search engine</li>
          </ul>
          <p>This data is associated with a randomly assigned cookie ID, not with your name or email. We do not enable Google's advertising features or demographic tracking. Google's own privacy policy governs how Google handles analytics data: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>
          <p>To opt out of Google Analytics across all sites, use the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.</p>

          <h3 id="cookies">Cookies</h3>
          <p>We use one category of cookies:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> (Google Analytics): Set by Google to distinguish unique visitors and sessions. These expire after 2 years of inactivity.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels, or third-party retargeting. You can disable cookies in your browser settings; the site will still function normally without them.</p>

          <h3 id="embedded-content">Embedded content</h3>
          <p>Some pages embed YouTube videos using the privacy-enhanced <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code> domain. YouTube may still set cookies when you interact with an embedded video. YouTube's privacy policy applies: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>

          <h3 id="what-we-do-not-collect">What we do not collect</h3>
          <p>We do not collect names, email addresses, phone numbers, or any information you don't explicitly send us. We have no account system, no login, no forms, and no comment sections. We do not collect information about what drugs you use or any other personally sensitive information.</p>

          <h2 id="affiliate-links">Affiliate links</h2>
          <p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. When you click an affiliate link and make a purchase, we may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. We have affiliate relationships with:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>DanceSafe</strong>: reagent test kits, fentanyl and xylazine test strips, earplugs, milligram scales, hydration packs, and other harm reduction supplies (<code>dancesafe.org/r/ravewellness/</code>)</li>
            <li><strong>Amazon Associates</strong>: supplements, naloxone, empty capsules and capsule fillers, home drug test kits, and other supplies DanceSafe does not carry (tag: <code>ravewellness01-20</code>)</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Affiliate relationships do not influence our recommendations. We only link to products that have a direct harm reduction purpose. Pages containing affiliate links display a disclosure near the relevant links.</p>

          <h2 id="hosting-and-infrastructure">Hosting and infrastructure</h2>
          <p>The site is hosted on <strong>Vercel</strong>. Vercel may log request metadata (IP address, timestamp, user agent) for security and abuse prevention purposes as standard web server infrastructure. Vercel's privacy policy: <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>.</p>

          <h2 id="data-sharing">Data sharing</h2>
          <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade personal data. We do not share data with advertisers. The only third parties that receive data from your visit are Google (Analytics) and Vercel (hosting), as described above.</p>

          <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
          <p>Because we do not collect identifiable personal information directly, we cannot look up or delete a record associated with your name. For data held by Google Analytics, you can use Google's tools to manage or delete your data at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com</a>.</p>
          <p>If you are in the EU or UK, Google Analytics data is processed under Google's data processing terms. If you are in California, the CCPA applies to data Google holds; Google's opt-out tools apply.</p>

          <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
          <p>This site contains information about controlled substances and is intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect data from anyone under 18.</p>

          <h2 id="changes-to-this-policy">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>If we make material changes to how we handle data, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. We will not retroactively weaken privacy protections for data already collected.</p>

          <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
          <p>Questions about this policy or data practices: <a href="mailto:hello@ravewellness.org">hello@ravewellness.org</a></p>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
